start water_cosmo

title "Water DFT energy with COSMO solvent (eps=78.4) — solvent starter template"

echo

# Water as both solute and solvent — useful as a sanity check that COSMO
# is wired correctly. Real workflows substitute the geometry and choose a
# solvent epsilon that matches the bulk medium.

geometry units angstroms noautosym
  O 0.0000  0.0000  0.1173
  H 0.0000  0.7572 -0.4692
  H 0.0000 -0.7572 -0.4692
end

basis
  * library def2-svp
end

charge 0

dft
  xc b3lyp
  iterations 200
  direct
end

# COSMO is NWChem's most common implicit-solvent model. epsilon=78.4 is
# bulk water at 298 K. Use rsolv=1.30 (default) for water; switch to
# rsolv=1.85 for non-protic solvents.
cosmo
  dielec 78.4
end

task dft energy

# After the run, check the COSMO surface charge convergence in the output —
# poorly converged surface charges often indicate the cavity overlaps a
# diffuse basis function or the geometry is too close to a discontinuity.
